{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHDZ4JByuYkSbJ8PYGW6Nz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gap hunt: C05 — Control dependency, model, and training changes\n2\t\n3\tA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\n4\tcheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\n5\tlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n6\t\n7\tFor each check, decide:\n8\t- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n9\t  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n10\t  Quote that line;\n11\t- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n12\t- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n13\t\n14\t**The requirement for C05:** Pin dependency versions. Where supported, also pin each model's base version, checkpoint or weights, and fine-tune or adapter version. Before promotion, link any changed training run, dataset, or training code or config to the model it produced and to its test results. Record the model version actually served, when the runtime or provider shares it, separately from the name you requested. Before loading weights, adapters, or datasets you host, check their signature against an approved signer (for example, with OpenSSF Model Signing). Also check their file format. Pickle-based formats can run code when loaded, so they need an approved exception and a scan. Test swapping a model, checkpoint, or adapter, and check that it triggers review and re-testing. Some remote services or names can change behind a fixed name. For those, record missing training and version details clearly. Watch available version metadata and provider notices, and decide when to re-test or stop using the model. A local config hash alone can't prove remote behavior is unchanged. A pinned snapshot fixes the weights, not the provider's serving systems, which can change under the same ID. Keep scheduled re-testing.\n15\t\n16\tIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n17\t`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t## C05.1\n21\t\n22\t**Check:** Dependency versions are pinned with exact versions or hashes in lockfiles, with no ranges or floating tags.\n23\t\n24\t**How to verify:** 1) Open every dependency file and lockfile (`requirements*.txt`, `poetry.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `go.sum`) plus Dockerfile `FROM` and install lines. 2) Look for ranges (`^`, `~`, `>=`, `*`), missing lockfiles, and floating tags. 3) Answer no if any dependency is unpinned, including install commands in Dockerfiles or CI scripts that bypass the lockfile.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:** package.json:17 — \"\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** Direct dependencies are pinned to exact versions (package.json:17-35), but no package-lock.json is in the tree though Dockerfile:4 and ci.yml:20 run npm ci with one. Transitive pins cannot be read.\n29\t\n30\t`package.json` lines 5–29 (cited lines marked >):\n31\t```\n32\t   5    \"type\": \"module\",\n33\t   6    \"engines\": {\n34\t   7      \"node\": \">=22.11\"\n35\t   8    },\n36\t   9    \"scripts\": {\n37\t  10      \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n38\t  11      \"start\": \"node dist/server.js\",\n39\t  12      \"reminders\": \"node dist/workers/reminders.js\",\n40\t  13      \"lint\": \"eslint src test\",\n41\t  14      \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n42\t  15    },\n43\t  16    \"dependencies\": {\n44\t  17>     \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\n45\t  18      \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n46\t  19      \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\": \"3.893.0\",\n47\t  20      \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\": \"3.893.0\",\n48\t  21      \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n49\t  22      \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.18.2\",\n50\t  23      \"fastify\": \"5.6.1\",\n51\t  24      \"jose\": \"6.1.0\",\n52\t  25      \"pino\": \"9.11.0\",\n53\t  26      \"undici\": \"7.16.0\",\n54\t  27      \"yaml\": \"2.8.1\",\n55\t  28      \"zod\": \"3.25.76\"\n56\t  29    },\n57\t```\n58\t\n59\t## C05.2\n60\t\n61\t**Check:** Model IDs in config are pinned snapshots (plus checkpoint, weights, and adapter versions where supported), not aliases such as 'latest'.\n62\t\n63\t**How to verify:** 1) Find every model ID in config, env files, and code defaults. 2) Follow env vars to their fallback value. 3) Answer no if any is an alias (`-latest`, undated name), falls back to one when unset, or leaves out the checkpoint, weights, or adapter version where one is used and the provider supports pinning it.\n64\t\n65\t**Reviewer's evidence:** src/config.ts:49 — \"export const AGENT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\";\"\n66\t\n67\t**Reviewer's note:** Both model ids are dated snapshots.\n68\t\n69\t`src/config.ts` lines 37–61 (cited lines marked >):\n70\t```\n71\t  37    onExceed: \"handoff_to_staff\";\n72\t  38  }\n73\t  39  \n74\t  40  function loadYaml<T>(rel: string): T {\n75\t  41    return parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, rel), \"utf8\")) as T;\n76\t  42  }\n77\t  43  \n78\t  44  export const policy = loadYaml<Policy>(\"config/policy.yaml\");\n79\t  45  export const allowlist = loadYaml<{ role: string; tools: AllowlistEntry[] }>(\"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\");\n80\t  46  export const budgets = loadYaml<Budgets>(\"config/budgets.yaml\");\n81\t  47  export const manifest = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"release/manifest.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n82\t  48  \n83\t  49> export const AGENT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\";\n84\t  50  export const CLASSIFIER_MODEL = \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\";\n85\t  51  \n86\t  52  export const env = {\n87\t  53    region: process.env.AWS_REGION ?? \"us-west-2\",\n88\t  54    controlTable: process.env.CONTROL_TABLE ?? \"clinic-agent-control\",\n89\t  55    budgetTable: process.env.BUDGET_TABLE ?? \"clinic-agent-budgets\",\n90\t  56    auditStream: process.env.AUDIT_STREAM ?? \"clinic-agent-audit\",\n91\t  57    smsSigningSecretArn: process.env.SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN ?? \"\",\n92\t  58    chatJwksUrl: process.env.CHAT_JWKS_URL ?? \"https://auth.northbay-clinics.example/.well-known/jwks.json\",\n93\t  59    chatIssuer: process.env.CHAT_ISSUER ?? \"https://auth.northbay-clinics.example/\",\n94\t  60    eligibilityUrl: process.env.ELIGIBILITY_URL ?? \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example/a2a\",\n95\t  61    eligibilityIssuer: process.env.ELIGIBILITY_ISSUER ?? \"https://eligibility.partners.northbay-clinics.example\",\n96\t```\n97\t\n98\t## C05.3\n99\t\n100\t**Check:** Self-hosted weights, adapters, and datasets have their signatures checked against an approved signer before loading, and loading stops if the check fails.\n101\t\n102\t**How to verify:** 1) Find load paths for self-hosted weights, adapters, and datasets. 2) Check a signature check against an approved signer (for example OpenSSF Model Signing, `cosign verify` with a pinned identity) runs before loading. 3) Answer no if any path skips it, any signer is accepted, or a failure is caught and loading continues. If nothing is self-hosted, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\n103\t\n104\t**Reviewer's evidence:** release/manifest.json:23 — \"\"adapter\": null,\"\n105\t\n106\t**Reviewer's note:** No self-hosted artifacts to sign-check.\n107\t\n108\t`release/manifest.json` lines 11–35 (cited lines marked >):\n109\t```\n110\t  11    },\n111\t  12    \"prompts\": [\n112\t  13      { \"path\": \"prompts/system.md\", \"sha256\": \"5d1e0c9b8a7f6e5d4c3b2a1908f7e6d5c4b3a291807f6e5d4c3b2a19087f6e5d\" },\n113\t  14      { \"path\": \"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\", \"sha256\": \"a3f9e1d7c5b3a1f9e7d5c3b1a9f7e5d3c1b9a7f5e3d1c9b7a5f3e1d9c7b5a3f1\" }\n114\t  15    ],\n115\t  16    \"models\": [\n116\t  17      {\n117\t  18        \"role\": \"agent\",\n118\t  19        \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n119\t