ving_stack\"]\n154\t  25      },\n155\t  26      {\n156\t  27        \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n157\t  28        \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n158\t  29        \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n159\t  30        \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n160\t  31        \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n161\t  32>       \"adapter\": null,\n162\t  33        \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n163\t  34      }\n164\t  35    ],\n165\t  36    \"tools\": {\n166\t  37      \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n167\t  38      \"mcpServers\": [\n168\t  39        {\n169\t  40          \"id\": \"ehr\",\n170\t  41          \"url\": \"https://ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example/mcp\",\n171\t  42          \"tlsCertSha256\": \"1f6a9c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e9b1d3f5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c1e3b5d7f9a\",\n172\t  43          \"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"\n173\t  44        }\n174\t```\n175\t\n176\t## C05.5\n177\t\n178\t**Check:** The model version the provider or runtime reports serving is recorded separately from the requested model name.\n179\t\n180\t**How to verify:** 1) Find model call sites and their response handling. 2) Check the served version from the response or runtime (for example the response `model` field) is stored in its own field. 3) Answer no if only the requested name is recorded, or the served field is filled with the requested value.\n181\t\n182\t**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/loop.ts:71 — \"servedModel: res.model,\"\n183\t\n184\t**Reviewer's note:** Served model is recorded separately.\n185\t\n186\t`src/agent/loop.ts` lines 59–83 (cited lines marked >):\n187\t```\n188\t  59        const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n189\t  60        const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n190\t  61        const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n191\t  62        const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n192\t  63        await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n193\t  64  \n194\t  65        const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n195\t  66        await audit.record({\n196\t  67          ...ident(),\n197\t  68          event: \"model.decision\",\n198\t  69          context: contextSize,\n199\t  70          detail: {\n200\t  71>           servedModel: res.model,\n201\t  72            stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n202\t  73            proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n203\t  74            span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n204\t  75          },\n205\t  76        });\n206\t  77  \n207\t  78        if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n208\t  79          const text = res.content\n209\t  80            .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n210\t  81            .map((b) => b.text)\n211\t  82            .join(\"\\n\")\n212\t  83            .slice(0, 320);\n213\t```\n214\t\n215\t## Your answer\n216\t\n217\tWrite this JSON to C05.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"C05\"):\n218\t```json\n219\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n220\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"C05.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n221\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n222\t```\n223\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n224\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"469bbcdb-b50c-4690-ae02-14012118afa4","uuid":"298eea76-9d3f-4282-af13-15f3a3ed094b","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:53:15.867Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-hpxxmwms/sheet.md","content":"# Gap hunt: C05 — Control dependency, model, and training changes\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for C05:** Pin dependency versions. Where supported, also pin each model's base version, checkpoint or weights, and fine-tune or adapter version. Before promotion, link any changed training run, dataset, or training code or config to the model it produced and to its test results. Record the model version actually served, when the runtime or provider shares it, separately from the name you requested. Before loading weights, adapters, or datasets you host, check their signature against an approved signer (for example, with OpenSSF Model Signing). Also check their file format. Pickle-based formats can run code when loaded, so they need an approved exception and a scan. Test swapping a model, checkpoint, or adapter, and check that it triggers review and re-testing. Some remote services or names can change behind a fixed name. For those, record missing training and version details clearly. Watch available version metadata and provider notices, and decide when to re-test or stop using the model. A local config hash alone can't prove remote behavior is unchanged. A pinned snapshot fixes the weights, not the provider's serving systems, which can change under the same ID. Keep scheduled re-testing.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## C05.1\n\n**Check:** Dependency versions are pinned with exact versions or hashes in lockfiles, with no ranges or floating tags.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open every dependency file and lockfile (`requirements*.txt`, `poetry.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `go.sum`) plus Dockerfile `FROM` and install lines. 2) Look for ranges (`^`, `~`, `>=`, `*`), missing lockfiles, and floating tags. 3) Answer no if any dependency is unpinned, including install commands in Dockerfiles or CI scripts that bypass the lockfile.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** package.json:17 — \"\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Direct dependencies are pinned to exact versions (package.json:17-35), but no package-lock.json is in the tree though Dockerfile:4 and ci.yml:20 run npm ci with one. Transitive pins cannot be read.\n\n`package.json` lines 5–29 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   5    \"type\": \"module\",\n   6    \"engines\": {\n   7      \"node\": \">=22.11\"\n   8    },\n   9    \"scripts\": {\n  10      \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n  11      \"start\": \"node dist/server.js\",\n  12      \"reminders\": \"node dist/workers/reminders.js\",\n  13      \"lint\": \"eslint src test\",\n  14      \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  15    },\n  16    \"dependencies\": {\n  17>     \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\n  18      \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n  19      \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\": \"3.893.0\",\n  20      \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\": \"3.893.0\",\n  21      \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n  22      \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.18.2\",\n  23   